  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two metallic blocks <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> of same area of cross-section are connected to each other (as shown in figure). If the thermal conductivity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> then the thermal conductivity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> will be : [Assume steady state heat conduction]</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/03fb5558-a997-4a49-b59e-ab8291a73a2f-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 88px;\" /></p>",
